0..71 Comment "// What a recursion handed through a higher-order function refuses. The"
72..148 Comment "// recursion\'s own parameter handed to `apply` or `applyAt` instantiates its"
149..227 Comment "// parameter or stage at that parameter\'s stage, which the claim does not take"
228..306 Comment "// (#393, #392). A helper whose signature names no type parameter and no stage"
307..382 Comment "// hands its argument on at no stage, and a helper with no recursion and no"
383..451 Comment "// stage opens none for its result to follow: the model\'s quantified"
452..528 Comment "// signatures lift both, `applyAt` the first and `predAt` the second. A call"
529..604 Comment "// whose arguments bound one stage binder where no stage fits is refused by"
605..682 Comment "// name, and so is a stage supplied by name, `applyAt[i = k]`, apart from the"
683..757 Comment "// one the arguments show or for a binder they do not show (#1227). Shared"
758..810 Comment "// with `../../model/data/sized-higher-order.gandr`."
812..854 Comment "// The naturals the recursions take apart."
855..861 Keyword "import"
862..863 StringLit "\""
863..895 StringLit "../../model/data/data-base.gandr"
895..896 StringLit "\""
896..897 Other ";"
